window.docContents[244].resolve({"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Proving-with-Tactics/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Proving-with-Tactics--Examples":{"contents":"The proofs below prove those same ten theorems again, now with tactics. Each can be read alongside the proof term of the previous section.\n\nExample 1. Implication is reflexive.\n\nexample (P : Prop) : P → P := by\n  intro h\n  exact h\n\n\nExample 2. A conjunction entails each conjunct.\n\nexample (P Q : Prop) : P ∧ Q → P := by\n  intro h\n  exact h.left\n\n\nExample 3. A disjunct entails the disjunction.\n\nexample (P Q : Prop) : P → P ∨ Q := by\n  intro h\n  exact Or.inl h\n\n\nExample 4. Anything follows from absurdity.\n\nexample (P : Prop) : False → P := by\n  intro h\n  exact False.elim h\n\n\nExample 5. Modus ponens, packaged as a single implication.\n\nexample (P Q : Prop) : (P → Q) ∧ P → Q := by\n  intro h\n  apply h.left\n  exact h.right\n\n\nExample 6. Disjunction commutes.\n\nexample (P Q : Prop) : P ∨ Q → Q ∨ P := by\n  intro h\n  cases h with\n  | inl hP => exact Or.inr hP\n  | inr hQ => exact Or.inl hQ\n\n\nExample 7. Double negation introduction.\n\nexample (P : Prop) : P → ¬¬P := by\n  intro hP hnP\n  exact hnP hP\n\n\nExample 8. Contraposition.\n\nexample (P Q : Prop) : (P → Q) → (¬Q → ¬P) := by\n  intro hPQ hnQ hP\n  exact hnQ (hPQ hP)\n\n\nExample 9. Double negation elimination, which needs classical reasoning.\n\nexample (P : Prop) : ¬¬P → P := by\n  intro h\n  apply Classical.byContradiction\n  intro hnP\n  exact h hnP\n\n\nExample 10. Currying turns a conjunctive hypothesis into nested implications.\n\nexample (P Q R : Prop) : (P ∧ Q → R) → (P → (Q → R)) := by\n  intro h hP hQ\n  exact h ⟨hP, hQ⟩\n\n\n","context":"Formal Software Verification\u0009Lecture 1: Motivation and Propositional Logic\u0009Proving with Tactics","header":"1.7.6. Examples","id":"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Proving-with-Tactics/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Proving-with-Tactics--Examples"}});